  body: |
    # ESA earnings and the separate permitted-work question

    ## Authored interpretation

    The source distinguishes the income effect of employed earnings for ESA(IR) from their relevance to permitted-work limits, including for ESA(Cont).

    ## Scope and boundaries

    DMG 49003–49004 do not support saying that work or earnings never matter for ESA(Cont). Work status, limits, exceptions and current New Style rules are not resolved or calculated here.

    ## Inspected source passages

    - [DMG 49003, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 49004, PDF page 3](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e6000e44a079b27f997f4e/dmg-Chap-49.pdf#page=3)
    - [DMG 48007, PDF page 5](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/5a8020bded915d74e33f89b8/dmgch48.pdf#page=5)

    ## Evidence and review status

    This is an unreviewed, model-assisted interpretation of selected passages in the frozen DWP guidance. It is an independent experimental publication, not an official DWP document, an entitlement decision or an executable benefits rule. ESA(Cont), ESA(IR), New Style ESA, UC and Pension Credit are not equated. The captured source contains historical, transitional and potentially superseded provisions; no complete or current legal rule set is claimed. Machine extraction can affect reading order, footnotes and characters. No visual PDF review or specialist acceptance is claimed.

    Source captured: 2026-09-15T19:45:30.556786Z. This is an acquisition time, not a publication, revision or commencement date. Source-stated dates retain their own role and precision.

